{
  "meta": {
    "version": "0.1",
    "last_updated": "2026-10-12",
    "notes": "Resilient-build explorer data (phase 1: energy and cost). Every figure is an indicative 2026 estimate marked for sourcing; the UI says so. Costs are hard construction cost, excluding land and soft costs. Added wall cost is per square foot of WALL over a 2021-code 2x6 wall; premium share of house is the cross-check band the computed premium must fall in. HERS equivalents bridge each archetype to the existing energy model (home.js annualEnergyCost) until a wall-by-wall heat-loss model replaces them. See docs/specs/RESILIENT_BUILD_SPEC.md and docs/SWISS_ENVELOPE_US_REFERENCE.md."
  },
  "geometry": {
    "wall_area_factor": {
      "1": 1.2,
      "2": 0.9
    },
    "window_area_pct": 15,
    "notes": "Exterior wall area as a multiple of floor area: a one-storey rectangle has more wall per floor; two storeys share a roof and a slab. Window area 15% of floor area is a common US design rule (IECC prescriptive path limits windows to 15% of wall area in some paths; 15% of floor area is a typical single-family outcome). Same convention as retrofit.js (roof ≈ 50% of living area)."
  },
  "windows": {
    "double_per_sqft_usd": {
      "low": 40,
      "high": 60
    },
    "triple_per_sqft_usd": {
      "low": 80,
      "high": 150
    },
    "notes": "Installed cost per square foot of window. Double-pane builder windows vs triple-pane tilt-turn (Alpen Tyrol, Zola, INTUS). Owner reports put Zola packages at $60–110/sq ft (dated).",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.phius.org/products/w-101007",
      "https://www.greenbuildingadvisor.com/question/help-me-choose-my-high-performance-windows-please"
    ]
  },
  "systems": {
    "erv_usd": {
      "low": 4000,
      "high": 9000
    },
    "heatpump_new_build_increment_usd": {
      "low": 2000,
      "high": 6000
    },
    "hpwh_new_build_increment_usd": {
      "low": 800,
      "high": 2000
    },
    "notes": "ERV: ducted energy-recovery ventilator installed (Zehnder ComfoAir Q class at the top of the range, Broan/Renewaire at the bottom). On a NEW build a heat pump replaces a furnace plus air conditioner the house would have needed anyway, so only the increment counts; on a retrofit (archetype C) the full measure cost from us-home-data.json measures applies via upgradeLedger.",
    "sources": [
      "https://zehnderamerica.com/",
      "https://www.energysage.com/heat-pumps/costs-and-benefits-air-source-heat-pumps"
    ]
  },
